From 4f13598efa5616b9f807aa4954484ec0992a8d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:00:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native query handlers and the full HTTP route table

Port chronik-indexer/src/query/{blocks,txs,group_history,group_utxos,
broadcast,tx_token_data,util}.rs and chronik-http handlers.rs with the
server.rs route table: blocks, headers, block txs, txs, raw txs,
tokens, unconfirmed txs, script/token-id/LOKAD-id history and UTXOs,
script batch utxos/summary (1-500 scripts), validate/broadcast with
token burn checks and finalization waits, and the plugin routes, which
answer exactly as Rust does with no plugins loaded. Query parameter
parsing, parse order, defaults and error texts follow Rust.

Handlers build their response plan under one indexer snapshot and make
Host calls (tx loads, headers, pre-consensus finality) after releasing
it. Mempool results are re-sorted big-endian to reproduce Rust's
output order.

Tests: 20 handler cases over a FakeHost chain with mempool, avalanche
finality, scripthash and SLP token flow, covering every route's success
and error paths (Rust has no tests in these modules).

Tier: eCash

